  "assumptions": [
    "Natural birth totals and first eligible home from existing catalogue; starting rent advance not deducted in this scenario model.",
    "Existing tech entry salary GH150; one real hour per attended shift on valid weekdays; no invented social income, top-ups, First Friend cash, salary bonuses or speculative trading partners.",
    "No promotions assumed: deliberately conservative. Existing salary/skill promotion rules are unit/integration tested separately.",
    "One active GH20 meal and GH8 data per visit, plus up to three GH22 offline meals per return; weekly rent and existing tax bands. Other transport is walking; discretionary luxury, loans, real payment and random medical/crime outcomes excluded.",
    "Managed business uses actual demandPeriod with transparent deterministic trial noise; daily visitors settle daily, casual visitors settle at two visits/week and lose periods beyond the 48-hour cap. Inventory purchases and till movements are tracked; retained stock is not cash.",
    "Equal-sized start cohorts compare paths; concentration below is not an estimate of the real player population or birth-odds distribution.",
    "Model is a budget stress test, not a full server/NPC/needs simulation. Missed rent is counted without modeling relocation after eviction. Different home choices, careers, play times and purchases materially change results."
  ],
