  "findings": [
    "The starts retain a substantial wealth gap. Wealth is not proof of a profitable operation.",
    "Pure social play with few paid shifts is not financially self-supporting under daily return food costs; existing offline food/rent bands are an approval topic, not silently changed.",
    "A stock-limited provision stall is supplementary income, not a replacement for early employment.",
    "Casual cadence benefits from capped offline meals but misses demand beyond 48 hours. Lower-rent home choices matter."
  ],
  "approvalRecommendations": [
    "Review offline-food burden and basic-career wage viability across all existing ranks before production; keep existing values until approved.",
    "Physical-device and live concurrency/load testing before release."
